From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Re-point X11 device guards from _DEVICE_ to _X11_

CIrrDeviceLinux.cpp/.h and six other files gate X11 device code on
`_IRR_COMPILE_WITH_X11_DEVICE_`. IrrCompileConfig.h line 105 defines
that macro unconditionally, while `NO_IRR_COMPILE_WITH_X11_` only
undefs the separate `_IRR_COMPILE_WITH_X11_` macro (line 189-190).
The guard is therefore always true and the X11 includes/calls leak
in even when the recipe passes NO_IRR_COMPILE_WITH_X11_:

  CIrrDeviceLinux.cpp:24:10: fatal error: 'X11/XKBlib.h' file not found
  COSOperator.cpp:89:23: error: member access into incomplete type
        'irr::CIrrDeviceLinux'

Re-point all 23 `_IRR_COMPILE_WITH_X11_DEVICE_` references across 9
files to `_IRR_COMPILE_WITH_X11_`, which the recipe-side NO_ macro
actually controls.

---
 source/Irrlicht/COSOperator.cpp              | 8 ++++----
 source/Irrlicht/COSOperator.h                | 2 +-
 source/Irrlicht/COpenGLDriver.cpp            | 12 ++++++------
 source/Irrlicht/COpenGLDriver.h              | 2 +-
 source/Irrlicht/COpenGLExtensionHandler.cpp  | 1 +-
 source/Irrlicht/COpenGLExtensionHandler.h    | 2 +-
 source/Irrlicht/CIrrDeviceLinux.cpp          | 2 +-
 source/Irrlicht/CIrrDeviceLinux.h            | 2 +-
 source/Irrlicht/Irrlicht.cpp                 | 2 +-
 9 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)

--- a/source/Irrlicht/COSOperator.cpp	2026-08-05 21:45:57.244087187 +0800
+++ b/source/Irrlicht/COSOperator.cpp	2026-08-05 21:45:57.740085156 +0800
